und = [o for o in sorted(tab) if max(tab[o]) - min(tab[o]) >= 1e-5]
P(">>> READ THE TABLE HONESTLY, INCLUDING THE ROW THAT BREAKS IT.")
P("    ORDERS %s ARE FULLY DETERMINED: every sector at those orders gives the same H_FULL to 1e-5"
  % det)
P("       -- order 1 and order 3 give a FULL BIT, order 5 gives ZERO.  %d of %d sectors."
  % (sum(len(tab[o]) for o in det), sum(len(tab[o]) for o in tab)))
P("    ORDER %s IS NOT: its %d sectors span [%.9f , %.9f], the whole range."
  % (und, sum(len(tab[o]) for o in und), min(min(tab[o]) for o in und), max(max(tab[o]) for o in und)))
P("")
P("    SO THE MAGNETIC CONNECTION ORDER IS A PARTIAL DISCRIMINATOR, NOT THE ANSWER.  My")
P("    identification, made on two sectors, survives on 16 of 36 and fails on the remaining 20.")
P("    THE INVENTION STAYS REFUTED.  I am NOT going hunting for the variable that splits the")
P("    order-2 group: with 128 points and a large predictor class, anything I found by looking")
P("    would be fitting, which is the one thing the principal asked this round to avoid.  The")
P("    order-2 split is logged as UNDETERMINED and handed to the next lane as a pre-registerable")
